# The trial of pod-supervise in podvm (T-060): crates/podvm-supervise keeps
# podvm's glue and calls the crate. Its lib.rs gives settings(store) (the
# store root, the store's `lock` for the table, the `podvm_containers` key,
# the `podvm_` names, `podvm ps -a`, EXIT_RUNTIME_ERROR) and keeps each verb
# with a &Store; `referencing` is `matching`. Its table.rs gives podvm's
# record fields (`Detail`: image, manifest_digest, rootfs, rung,
# userland_exec, completion, completion_degraded; Container =
# Container<Detail>), the paths and the table calls with a &Store, and keeps
# the ownership memo (table/memo.rs). Its launcher.rs is podvm's entry, run
# in the launcher of the crate: the memo, the devices, the root, the plan,
# the image hold, the rung. launcher/supervise.rs leaves podvm. podvm-image
# re-exports pod_supervise::lock::Lock as store::Lock, and its try_lock_at
# and lock_at map a Failure to podvm's errors and give the T-0215 note in
# test builds. Each podcrates tag moves to v0.8.0. Six citations of the
# record follow the moved lines.
# podvm's tests of each touched crate and of the lifecycle through the
# binary (the live clauses skip with their reason where no image can be
# pulled); clippy of the workspace and rustfmt of the touched crates, as
# podvm's gate.yml runs them; the runtime-state rows; podvm's record gate;
# each Rust toolchain of the workflows against the rust-version of
# podcrates; and the binary `podvm` for x86_64 musl, with podcrates' static
# check.
cargo test -q -p podvm-supervise
cargo test -q -p podvm-image
cargo test -q -p podvm --bin podvm
cargo test -q -p podvm --test store_gates
cargo test -q -p podvm --test detached_stdio
cargo test -q -p podvm --test qol
cargo clippy -q --workspace --all-targets -- -D warnings
cargo fmt -p podvm-supervise -p podvm-image -p podvm --check
cargo build -q -p podvm --bin podvm
# podvm's gate finds the root of the repository from the path of its binary,
# so it runs from target/release/, with document-state beside it (gate.yml).
cargo build -q --release -p podvm-gate && cargo build -q --release -p podvm-release --bin document-state
mkdir -p target/release && cp "${CARGO_TARGET_DIR:-target}/x86_64-unknown-linux-musl/release/podvm-gate" "${CARGO_TARGET_DIR:-target}/x86_64-unknown-linux-musl/release/document-state" target/release/
# docs/runtime-state.md lists each direct git or registry dependency with its
# locked version. The patch gives the rows of the git form (pod-core,
# pod-hostprobe, pod-proxy, pod-supervise, pod-term and pod-tls at 0.8.0);
# the trial's path form has no row for them. Each other row of the patch
# must be the generated one.
grep -v '^| .pod-' docs/runtime-state.md > target/runtime-state.patch.md && python3 scripts/document-state.py --write && grep -v '^| .pod-' docs/runtime-state.md | diff target/runtime-state.patch.md -
./target/release/podvm-gate
python3 -I "$PODCRATES/scripts/check-consumer-toolchains.py"
sh "$PODCRATES/scripts/check-static.sh" "${CARGO_TARGET_DIR:-target}/x86_64-unknown-linux-musl/debug/podvm"
